{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Follow-up per operator ruling (a bug fix may not add a config key): Gerrit 3332 removes compact.worker_log / REBAR_COMPACT_WORKER_LOG entirely and decides the sweep log at the call site. The MCP transition_ticket tool pins the private library kwarg _sweep_log=\"stderr\" (same pattern as _creation_channel=\"mcp\"); rebar.transition -> transition_compute -> close_ticket -> maybe_compact -> _spawn_detached_sweep carries it. The CLI and direct library callers keep the store's .rebar/logs/compact-worker.log. No new mechanism of any kind (check_mechanism_delta --check exits 0, stale=0, so no baseline change). Removed: schema field + section validator + both markers, compose and mcp_run_new env, docs/config.md entry, regenerated config-reference/env-vars/config_surface golden. Tests first: MCP close spawns a sweep with stderr fd 2 and no log file; CLI close's sweep stderr is the store log file; key absent from the config surface. Before: 2 failed, 1 passed (CLI path was already the default). After: pass. Blue-green test now proves the tool pin -> journald driver/tag on the replacement container chain. make verify passed (20844 + 202 integration passed)."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793902162906479001,"uuid":"88c1f4f8-57a2-4d3e-8bac-447ba980d06e"}